&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;BitGo is the leading infrastructure provider of digital asset solutions, delivering custody, wallets, staking, trading, financing, and settlement services from regulated cold storage. Since our founding in 2013, we have focused on enabling our clients to securely navigate the digital asset space. With a global presence and multiple Trust companies, BitGo serves thousands of institutions, including many of the industry&#39;s top brands, exchanges, and platforms, and millions of retail investors worldwide. As the operational backbone of the digital economy, BitGo handles a significant portion of Bitcoin network transactions and is the largest independent digital asset custodian, and staking provider, in the world. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://www.bitgo.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://www.bitgo.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;www.bitgo.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced, hands-on Onboarding Manager to own and drive BitGo’s client onboarding function for our MAS-regulated Singapore entity. Reporting to BitGo’s APAC Managing Director, this role will own the end-end client lifecycle; including client onboarding, ongoing due diligence, periodic reviews and off-boarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a player/coach role where you will manage and mentor an Onboarding Associate while remaining deeply hands-on in day-to-day execution. You will own and manage onboarding cases directly, and help establish strong operating standards across the function. You will have the opportunity to shape BitGo Singapore’s onboarding operating model as the business continues to scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong KYC/KYB expertise and a solid understanding of MAS regulatory requirements paired with commercial and operational judgement. You are resourceful, pragmatic, and creative in solving problems, comfortable owning complex cases end to end, and able to find practical ways forward when the path is not always clear. You partner effectively with cross-functional stakeholders, challenge inefficient ways of working, and thrive in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Onboarding and Offboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and progress onboarding applications end to end, ensuring high execution quality, robust documentation and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage onboarding queues and priorities to maintain strong throughput and adherence to service level expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify information gaps and manage requests for information efficiently to minimize unnecessary client friction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Compliance on cases requiring additional review or escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own client offboarding end to end, including sanctions and risk driven terminations, dormant and inactive account closures, and coordination of account wind-down with Operations and Compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and manage client-facing exit communications, ensuring exits are executed cleanly, defensibly, and with appropriate documentation and record retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales, Customer Success, Solutions Engineering, Operations, Compliance, and other cross-functional stakeholders to move clients through onboarding effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate onboarding requirements and blockers clearly to internal stakeholders and help drive cases toward resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance regulatory and risk requirements with commercial priorities and client experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence, Controls and Assurance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and continuously improve onboarding processes, workflows, controls, and operating standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Data Science and Analytics, Compliance, and Operations teams to improve onboarding systems and workflow logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of onboarding quality assurance practices and scalable service level frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, track, and report onboarding metrics including turnaround time and backlog aging and use them to drive improvements in efficiency and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audit and regulatory examinations, including producing onboarding and CDD files for sampling, participating in process walkthroughs, and evidencing controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own remediation of audit and review findings relating to onboarding, tracking actions through to closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the APAC onboarding function as a whole, providing guidance and subject matter expertise to colleagues handling onboarding cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish high standards for execution, ownership, documentation, and client experience across the APAC onboarding function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example as a hands-on operator, taking ownership of outcomes rather than simply managing workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in client onboarding, KYB/AML operations, financial crime operations, or a closely related function in the fintech, digital assets or payments industry; 1–2 years of experience leading or owning an onboarding function is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of MAS’ regulatory requirements and expectations around KYB, corporate structures, beneficial ownership, and AML onboarding processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting external audits or regulatory reviews, including evidencing controls and remediating findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial awareness and ability to balance risk requirements with onboarding efficiency and client experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management and communication skills with the ability to work effectively across Sales, Operations, Compliance, and other teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage escalations and make sound decisions in complex or ambiguous situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong critical thinking, problem solving, pattern recognition, and project management skills, with excellent attention to detail, organization, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment where processes and requirements continue to evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive mindset with a track record of identifying problems, challenging inefficient processes, and driving improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mandarin language skills will be a significant advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join BitGo?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Disrupting an industry takes vision, innovation, passion, technical chops, drive to deliver, collaboration, and execution. Join a team of great people who strive for excellence and personify our corporate values of ownership, craftsmanship, and open communication. We are looking for new colleagues who bring innovative ways of thinking and problem solving, and who want to be part of the team that changes the world’s financial markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here are some of the benefits of working at BitGo:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base salary, bonus, and stock options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer equipment to suit your needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great colleagues and inspiring startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;BitGo is the leading infrastructure provider of digital asset solutions, delivering custody, wallets, staking, trading, financing, and settlement services from regulated cold storage. Since our founding in 2013, we have focused on enabling our clients to securely navigate the digital asset space. With a global presence and multiple Trust companies, BitGo serves thousands of institutions, including many of the industry&#39;s top brands, exchanges, and platforms, and millions of retail investors worldwide. As the operational backbone of the digital economy, BitGo handles a significant portion of Bitcoin network transactions and is the largest independent digital asset custodian, and staking provider, in the world. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://www.bitgo.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://www.bitgo.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;www.bitgo.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;BitGo is the leader in digital asset financial services, providing institutional investors with liquidity, custody, and security solutions. Founded in 2013, BitGo pioneered the multi-signature wallet and is the first digital asset company to focus exclusively on serving institutional clients.&amp;nbsp; Active in both centralized and decentralized finance, BitGo offers market leading trading, lending, and borrowing services through its prime brokerage services and acts as the custodian for WBTC, the leading global stablecoin for Bitcoin. In 2020, BitGo launched BitGo Portfolio and Tax, providing clients with a full-stack solution for digital assets. In 2018, it launched BitGo Trust Company, the first qualified custodian purpose-built for storing digital assets. BitGo processes approximately 20% of all global Bitcoin transactions, and supports over 600 coins and tokens. BitGo provides the security and operational backbone for more than 1500 institutional clients in 50 countries, including many regulated entities and the world’s top cryptocurrency exchanges and platforms.&amp;nbsp; BitGo is backed by Goldman Sachs, Craft Ventures, Digital Currency Group, DRW, Galaxy Digital Ventures, Redpoint Ventures, and Valor Equity Partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The BitGo Prime team is a dynamic, high performing group that provides critical operational service to our institutional trading, lending, and borrowing clients in partnership with our Trust custody and compliance entity; global account managers and salespeople; and finance and accounting. Our extended unit consists of a diverse group of trading, lending, and KYC/AML professionals with extensive backgrounds in traditional and crypto-finance, including front, middle, and back office.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Prime Client Services Associate will be responsible for managing business operations for BitGo Prime’s digital asset trading and financing services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage BitGo Prime’s trade and settlement workflows including trade entry, asset transfers, reporting and reconciliation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Prime’s business team to maintain optimal funding across various trading venues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First line of support for trading or financing operations related enquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead process improvements, identify gaps, recommend improvements and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing efforts for all enhancements of proprietary systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce daily, weekly and monthly reporting for internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Sales and Client Services team with on-boarding new counterparties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying operational risks, introduce operational controls and document policies &amp;amp; procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the product/engineering team to improve our products and services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain relationships with clients, exchanges, liquidity providers and third party providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date about market trends, opportunities, risks and new projects, with a passion for the digital asset industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BitGo is looking for people who are passionate about their craft, take full ownership for their work and projects, and believe in transparent and collaborative culture with the goal of making BitGo successful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incredible attention to detail and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to effectively interact with others in a pleasant, professional manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and ability to understand assets flows and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have previous middle or back-office experience in a financial services Trading, stock loan, FX experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and interacting with clients is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortably manage competing priorities in a fast-moving, dynamic start-up environment&lt;/li&gt;
